VERDICT: PASS on the measurable half; mirror-port delivery UNVERIFIED.
===========================================================================
  Mirror session configured and confirmed:
      Mirror Test Port Name: port3.0.2 | Mirror option: Enabled
      Mirror direction: both           | Monitored Port Name: port2.0.2
  ACL rule matched: copy-to-mirror ipv6 2001:db8:a::/64 any -- Packet Hits: 10

  "Verify also forwarded in hardware"   -> PASS
      base 10/10 forwarded, with copy-to-mirror applied still 10/10.
      This is the half that distinguishes copy-to-mirror from send-to-cpu
      (T940, which drops to 0/10) -- so the actions are demonstrably
      different, not both no-ops.

  "Verify traffic sent to mirror port"  -> NOT VERIFIED
      port3.0.2 output counters stayed 0 packets / 0 bytes across the run.
      The mirror destination has NO CABLE -- it is the IE520's only spare
      copper port (each member has exactly one; port1.0.2 -> x230,
      port2.0.2 -> tb470 eth2, port4.0.2 -> 4050 LAG). A link-down port
      cannot transmit, so mirrored frames have nowhere to go and no counter
      moves. This is a bench limitation, not a product result.
      TO CLOSE THIS: cable tb470 eth1 (or any NIC) to port3.0.2 and re-run --
      the mirrored copies would then be capturable directly.
